# Central Relay Implementation Worklog

## Overview

This document tracks the implementation progress of the Central Relay service as detailed in the Central_Relay_Implementation_Plan.md document.

## Phase 1: Architecture and Configuration Setup ✅

### 1.1 Directory Structure ✅

Created the basic directory structure for the agent-tunnel-registry service:
```
agent-tunnel-registry/
├── server.js                 # Main application entry point
├── config.js                 # Configuration (ports, etc.)
├── api/
│   ├── index.js              # Main API router
│   ├── registrationRoutes.js # Routes for /register, /nodes
│   └── uriRoutes.js          # Routes for /uri/*
├── registry/
│   └── registryManager.js    # Logic for storing and retrieving node info
├── tunneling/
│   ├── controlListener.js    # TCP server for internal nodes' control connections
│   ├── publicRelayListener.js # TCP server for external clients to connect for relay
│   └── tunnelManager.js      # Manages active tunnels and data piping
├── stun/
│   └── stunServer.js         # STUN server for NAT traversal assistance
├── package.json              # Node.js dependencies and project metadata
└── README.md                 # Documentation
```

### 1.2 Package.json Configuration ✅

Created package.json with all required dependencies for the tunnel registry service.

### 1.3 Configuration Updates ✅

Updated the Go configuration in `config/config.go` to include settings for Node.js services and the tunnel client:

- Added `NodeJSServicesConfig` struct for Root/Root nodes
- Added `TunnelClientConfig` struct for Bootnodes and Peers
- Updated the main `Config` struct to include these new configurations

